<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman sees lower growth for EDS.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman sees lower growth for EDS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said it is projecting lower long-term secular growth in earnings per share for Electronic Data Systems Corp after the company guided Wall Street analysts' profit estimates lower at the first day of a two-day analyst meeting in Dallas.</p>
<p>-- It sees growth of 12 to 14 percent, down from its earlier estimate of 14 to 16 percent.  It reiterated a neutral rating and a 12-month price target range of $36 to $40.</p>
</text>
